From 738ce3b3020b3950c48ce3122a08f32af531d4fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikai <mikai@local>
Date: Sat, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aji: managed prepared-plan admission, stream control, source-shape transform and factory capability query

Additive prepared-plan v1 exports (aji_native_create_prepared,
aji_native_apply_prepared, aji_native_control_on_stream) over the existing
ABI-8/v2 snapshot/control, plus the managed source-shape transform. A plan
names owned absolute engine/model paths and their expected SHA-256 digests;
identity, device, runtime, geometry and cadence are validated and the digests
are compared BEFORE any deserialize, with no trtexec, cache key, legacy path
fallback, live build or file deletion. The coded source frame is cropped and
then rotated on the GPU (aji_run_yuv_crop_rotate) into a display-size frame
before any pre-resize, tensor binding or pad; odd coded sizes, odd crop
offsets and odd crop extents are mapped (4:2:0 chroma by whole pairs, ceil on
an odd extent) rather than refused, and the oriented geometry is what the
stages and the snapshot output report. Admission is transactional, suspend
releases the loaded resources and resume revalidates the retained plan, and
drain orders on the caller's stream.

Additive factory capability query (aji_native_query_factory), a standalone
optional backend export (aji_native_backend_query_factory) over its own query
protocol v1. It answers from the actually adopted, borrowed CUDA context and
never creates one: the real device UUID/SM are read through cuCtxGetDevice /
cuDeviceGetUuid, and the real TensorRT runtime factory is initialized and
destroyed, with the exact loaded runtime token and the backend's truly
compiled roles reported. A failed context, backend or runtime, or a schema
mismatch, is an observed-unavailable result named in reasonKey/reason and
never a true claim derived from export presence, preferences, filenames or
manifests. A backend without the export is refused by name and the legacy
ABI-8/v2 snapshot/control and prepared-plan calls keep working. No model,
engine, network, inference, build or cache path is touched.

native/include/aji_native.h is supplied by the build's include path (it is
not part of this inference source tree); this patch touches src/ only.

Apply after 0001-content-addressed-cache-and-prepared-only.patch and
0002-native-snapshot-and-control.patch against the pinned source.

---
